 "description": "This is the first deck I've ever submitted, and to be honest I've never really played outside of a circle of a few friends and I don't use virtual cards...yet.  I have no idea how this deck would do in a tournament, so any advice would be greatly appreciated.",
 "strategy": "My strategy is fairly simple.  I use The Signal as a starting interrupt and bring out Haven on Rendezvous point.  I do this so I can quickly deploy large amounts of starships and pilots.  This way when I flip Hidden Base, usually in 4 or 5 turns, it is very difficult for my opponent to keep up in space.  I also put mercenary armor and undercover on Leia RP to help cancel a couple force drains if I can’t do so with Rebel Fleet or the objective card.\n\nI'm really curious to see if this deck is remotely tournament caliber.  Opinions and advice would be great! Thanks.",
